# tw_raw_t Demo

This project provides `tw_raw_t`, a tool for reading CTW_Raw/TW_Raw records and outputting raw records, HTTP replies, or HTTP bodies.

## Project Layout

- `src/`: source code and `Makefile`
- `bin/`: compiled executable copied by `make`
- `TWFormat.pdf`: TW raw format reference

## Build

Requirements:

- `g++`
- `zlib` (linked with `-lz`)

From the project root:

```bash
make -C src
```

After build, the executable is available at:

- `src/tw_raw_t`
- `bin/tw_raw_t`

## Quick Runnable Test

Run this command in the `src/` directory:

```bash
cat /tmp/Downloads/Web_Raw.M201401.0001 | ./tw_raw_t --one-by-one
```

Notes:

- Input is read from standard input.
- `--one-by-one` writes each record to a separate file.
- Default output names look like `1.raw`, `2.raw`, `3.raw`, ...

## Common Options

- `--num=N`: process at most `N` records
- `--one-by-one`: write one output file per record
- `--package`: output records in `length + content` package format (conflicts with `--one-by-one`)
- `--http-reply`: output HTTP reply only (without TW_Raw outer headers)
- `--body-only`: output HTTP body only
- `--prefix=URL_PREFIX`: keep records whose URL starts with this prefix (can be repeated)
- `--select=FILE`: read selected URLs from a file (one URL per line)
- `-h` / `--help`: print help message

## More Examples

Extract at most 4 pages and output body-only files one by one:

```bash
cat Web_Raw.M201311.0001 | ./bin/tw_raw_t --num=4 --body-only --one-by-one
```

Show help:

```bash
./bin/tw_raw_t --help
```

